# Basalt prototype action plan

Goal: finish the Obsidian-light prototype: public profiles and notes, owner-only
editing, markdown notes, wiki-style links, and a link graph. Keep the current
stack; no rewrite.

Decisions:

- Public read, private write. Anyone can view public profiles, trees, notes, and
  graphs, including other users' content.
- Cross-user references are allowed in links. Cross-user edits are not.
- Notes get `is_private`; private notes are hidden from non-owners. Folders have
  no privacy flag.
- Logout clears the session but stays on the current URL. A public note stays
  visible read-only; a private note redirects to the profile root.
- Target API is `src/server/routes/route_plan` (REST). Current server routes are
  the pre-migration API.
- `npm run init:db` is destructive. Do not run it on the current database.
  Apply schema changes with SQL and regenerate kanel models.

## Phase 0 — Stabilize current app (done)

- [x] `src/client/components/App.tsx`: auth bootstrap runs once per load.
- [x] `src/client/components/Root.tsx`: declarative `<Navigate replace>`.
- [x] `src/client/components/NavigationBar.tsx`: logout clears Redux without
      navigating; failures are visible.
- [x] `src/client/components/FolderTree.tsx`: create/delete controls are gated
      by ownership; delete clicks no longer toggle rows; errors are shown;
      failed loads do not wipe the tree.
- [x] `src/server/routes/folder.ts`: folder update uses `getFolder`; missing
      returns and folder wording fixed.
- [x] `src/server/models/links.ts`: empty link lists are skipped; writes are
      scoped by user and wrapped in a transaction.
- [x] `src/server/routes/helpers.ts`: zero-weight graph edges are dropped.
- [x] `src/client/api.ts`: requests throw `ApiError` with server messages; dead
      status checks removed.
- [x] `src/server/auth.ts`: JWT payload is parsed through `User`, so the bcrypt
      hash is no longer signed; cookie is `sameSite: "lax"`.
- [x] `src/server/main.ts`: Zod-aware error middleware; invalid input returns
      `400` JSON.
- [x] Note and folder writes verify row ownership and return `403` for other
      users.
- [x] Auth forms, tree, note save, and graph load surface errors.
- [x] Added `npm run typecheck` and `npm run check`; nodemon watches schemas and
      config.
- [x] Verified: typecheck, build, anonymous read, empty-link note creation,
      cross-user note/folder writes return `403`, invalid login returns `400`,
      JWT excludes `encrypted_password`.

## Phase 1 — Private notes schema

- [ ] Back up the database:
      `pg_dump -h localhost -U basalt basalt > /tmp/opencode/basalt-backup.sql`
- [ ] Apply the non-destructive migration:
      `ALTER TABLE notes ADD COLUMN is_private boolean NOT NULL DEFAULT false;`
- [ ] Update `src/extra/init_db.ts` so the canonical schema includes
      `is_private`.
- [ ] Extract the kanel generation call from `init_db.ts` into
      `src/extra/gen_models.ts`; add `npm run gen:models` that regenerates
      `src/server/models/generated` from the live DB without dropping tables.
- [ ] Run `npm run gen:models`.
- [ ] Add `is_private: z.boolean()` to `Note` in `src/schemas/types.ts`.
      `CreateNote`/`UpdateNote` inherit it.
- [ ] Verify the new column, generated types, typecheck, and existing notes.

## Phase 2 — REST API migration

Implement `src/server/routes/route_plan`:

- [ ] `POST /api/session`, `DELETE /api/session`.
- [ ] `POST /api/users`, `GET /api/users`, `GET /api/users/me`,
      `GET /api/users/:user_id`, `/tree`, `/graph`.
- [ ] `POST /api/notes`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/notes/:note_id`.
- [ ] `POST /api/folders`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/folders/:folder_id`.
- [ ] Owner comes from the session on writes; never from the request body.
- [ ] Enforce ownership with `where("user_id", "=", req.user.id)` in Kysely for
      update/delete, not only in route checks.
- [ ] Add one Express error middleware. Return `400` validation, `401`
      unauthenticated write, `403` non-owner, `404` missing, `409` duplicate
      title/name.
- [ ] Update `src/client/api.ts` to the new endpoints and `PATCH` updates.
- [ ] Add `getFolder` and `updateFolder` client functions.
- [ ] Verify all existing flows after migration.

## Phase 3 — Privacy and logout behavior

- [ ] Tree reads accept optional auth: owner sees private notes; everyone else
      gets public notes only.
- [ ] `GET /notes/:note_id`: private notes return `404` to non-owners; owner
      sees them.
- [ ] Graph: owner includes links from own private notes; other viewers exclude
      them.
- [ ] Add an owner-only private checkbox in the note editor.
- [ ] Show a lock indicator for private notes in the owner's tree.
- [ ] On login/logout, refetch tree and graph so privacy visibility updates.
- [ ] Logout keeps the current URL and content when the note is public; the UI
      becomes read-only and the navbar switches to login/signup.
- [ ] Logout while viewing an owned private note clears it and redirects to the
      profile root.
- [ ] Verify: Bob cannot see Alice's private note in her tree or by direct URL;
      Alice's public note stays open after logout; Alice's private note
      redirects after logout; Bob links to Alice's public note successfully.

## Phase 4 — Navigation, editor, and layout

- [ ] Replace title-path parsing with ID routes:
      `/u/:username`, `/u/:username/notes/:note_id`.
- [ ] Tree rows navigate by ID; folder rows only expand/collapse.
- [ ] Build canonical `path` on the server from parent + title; stop accepting
      client-supplied paths.
- [ ] Replace `contentEditable` with a markdown textarea and preview toggle or
      split view.
- [ ] Add note title editing, dirty state, `Ctrl+S`, and delete confirmation.
- [ ] Add folder rename/move and note move if cheap; otherwise defer.
- [ ] Add a three-column layout and basic CSS: tree, note, optional side panel.
- [ ] Add active-note highlight, auto-expand, loading/empty/error states.

## Phase 5 — Links and graph

- [ ] Parse links with `marked` tokens instead of the broad
      `\(([^()]+)\)` regex.
- [ ] Keep `[label](target)` for MVP; add `[[Title]]` only if cheap.
- [ ] Resolve targets to canonical note paths; keep unresolved links visible.
- [ ] Graph endpoint: include every note as a point, deduplicate edges, keep
      isolated notes.
- [ ] Build the graph page using the existing `Graph.tsx` physics and SVG or
      canvas rendering.
- [ ] Clicking a node opens its note; label nodes by title/path.
- [ ] Optional: backlinks panel using the `links` table.

## Phase 6 — Finish

- [ ] Visible form validation: required names/passwords, password mismatch,
      duplicate-name conflict.
- [ ] Add a 404 route and bad-ID handling.
- [ ] Add a README with Postgres setup, `.env`, run commands, and the
      `init:db` warning.
- [ ] Optional demo seed script.
- [ ] Add `npm run check` = `tsc -p src/client --noEmit && vite build`.
- [ ] Optional `node --test` tests for `genFolder`, `genGraph`, and link parsing.
- [ ] Only after the MVP: search, tags, import/export, dark theme, graph zoom,
      deployment hardening.

## Definition of done

A new user can sign up, create folders and notes, write markdown with links,
edit/delete content, browse their tree, view a graph, and log out. Public notes
remain readable anonymously and by other users. Private notes stay owner-only.
Owners can edit; everyone else is read-only. `npx tsc -p src/client --noEmit`
and `npm run build` pass.
